  "scope": "Textual PID assignment/allocator-call and TxS initialization/reset inventory; raw word writes, aliases and generated variants need separate review. Not an exhaustive semantic proof.",
  "findings": [
    "Four regular allocator callsites in mac/mt_mac.c are covered by the checked allocator conversion.",
    "Short templates in mt7603/mt7628/mt7636 use logical PID_DATA_AMPDU=2, not255. MT7603 is the board-relevant case.",
    "Long special info->PID direct assignment is inside literal if(0) under WH_EZ_SETUP; cannot treat arbitrary future direct assignment as covered.",
    "InitTxSTypeTable zeroes all slots; permanent allocator exclusion does not depend on slot initialization or cursor.",
    "os/linux/diag.c pid fields are process IDs, not wire TxS IDs."
  ],
